# Permanent Project Rules

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind CSS in /client
- Node.js + Express + TypeScript + MongoDB (Mongoose) in /server

## Rules
- Inspect only files relevant to the current task. Never scan the whole project.
- Make targeted edits. Never rewrite whole files unless asked.
- Do not add dependencies without asking me first.
- No `any` types. Validate all API input with Zod.
- Never hardcode secrets; use environment variables and keep .env.example updated.
- Express structure: routes → controllers → services → models. Business logic lives only in /server.
- Next.js calls the Express API; do not duplicate backend logic in Next.js route handlers.
- Handle loading, error and empty states in every UI.
- After each task, run type-check and lint, then report: changed files, what was done, and anything unfinished.
- Keep replies short. No long explanations unless I ask.
